---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../site.config.js';
const updated = 'August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, which is almost nothing, and exactly what our host sees.">
  <main class="prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="dek">Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <p>
      This page describes what actually happens on this site, not what a template
      says usually happens. If anything here does not match the site's real
      behaviour, that is a bug — please tell us.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect about you: nothing</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts, no logins, no analytics, no advertising pixels, and
      no tracking of any kind. We do not know who you are, we do not know you
      visited, and we could not tell you how many people used a calculator today.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens to the numbers you type in</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculator runs entirely inside your browser. Your weight, height,
      age, sex, body-fat percentage and measurements are used to compute a result
      on your own device and are discarded when you close or reload the page.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Specifically, this information:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>is never transmitted to us or to anyone else,</li>
      <li>is never written into the page's web address, so it cannot leak through
        a shared link, browser history, or a referrer header,</li>
      <li>is never saved to your device between visits,</li>
      <li>is never combined, sold, or shared.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This is a deliberate design decision. Health measurements are sensitive, and
      the most reliable way to protect sensitive data is not to receive it.
    </p>

    <h2>Our host, and what it can see</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served by {LEGAL.host}. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
      the technical details necessary to deliver a page to you — your IP address,
      the time, the page requested, and your browser's user-agent string. That
      processing happens at Cloudflare's edge, not by us, and we do not use it for
      analytics, profiling, or anything connected to what you enter in a
      calculator.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare's security features may set a strictly necessary cookie on your
      device — typically <code>__cf_bm</code>, used for bot detection. It is a
      short-lived session cookie, it is not set by us, it holds no identifier
      belonging to this site, and Cloudflare states it is not used to track people
      between sites. If a security challenge is shown, a <code>cf_clearance</code>
      cookie may also be set to remember that you passed it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We set no cookies of our own</strong>, and there is nothing on this
      site that requires your consent to store or read information for our
      purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts are served from this site's own domain rather than a third-party font
      service, so loading a page does not announce your visit to anyone else. No
      analytics provider, tag manager, or advertising network is loaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some pages link out to other websites — research papers, retailers,
      reference material. Once you follow a link you are on someone else's site,
      and their practices apply rather than ours.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some outbound product links are affiliate links, marked where they appear.
      If you buy through one we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. The
      retailer will know you arrived from here; they will not learn anything you
      entered into a calculator, because we never had it. See our
      <a href="/ad-disclosure/">advertising disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      These calculators are built for adults aged 18 and over, and the site is not
      directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone —
      of any age — because we do not collect information at all.
    </p>
  <h2>If you are in California</h2>
  <p>
    We operate from {LEGAL.state}. The California Consumer Privacy Act gives residents
    the right to know what personal information a business collects, to have it deleted,
    to correct it, and to opt out of its sale or sharing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our answer to all of these is the same, and it is unusually short: we collect no
    personal information, so there is none to disclose, delete, or correct. We have never
    sold or shared personal information, and we have no mechanism capable of doing so —
    there is no database, no analytics provider, and no advertising network on this site.
    That includes the specific meaning "sharing" carries under California law, which covers
    passing information to advertisers for cross-context behavioural advertising.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we collect nothing, a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal from your
    browser has nothing to act on here. There is no opt-out to exercise, and no preference
    for us to record.
  </p>
  <p>
    To have any of the above confirmed in writing, email
    <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a> with
    <em>California privacy request</em> in the subject line. We will reply in writing. We
    will not ask you to verify your identity first, because we would have nothing to match
    it against.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in the UK or the European Economic Area</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated from {LEGAL.country} and is not directed at the UK or the EEA,
    but it is reachable from both. The UK GDPR and EU GDPR give people rights of access,
    rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability over personal data held
    about them.
  </p>
  <p>
    We hold no personal data, so those rights have nothing to attach to. The only personal
    data processed in connection with your visit is what our host handles to deliver the
    page — your IP address and request metadata, described above — and that is processed by
    Cloudflare under its own policies, not ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Requests may be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>


    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy laws in {LEGAL.country} and elsewhere give people rights to access,
      correct, or delete personal information held about them. We hold none, so
      there is nothing to access, correct, or delete. If you would like that
      confirmed in writing, email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>
      and we will confirm it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this site ever adds analytics, advertising, or any feature that stores
      your information, this page will be updated before that feature ships and
      the change noted here rather than made quietly.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
